1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:08,070
scale=-1:H works on some videos.

2
00:00:08,070 --> 00:00:15,550
On others it crashes. Why?

3
00:00:15,550 --> 00:00:22,410
1920x1080 to height 720: 1280x720.

4
00:00:22,410 --> 00:00:32,010
Exit code 0. 10 frames on disk.

5
00:00:32,010 --> 00:00:43,200
1000x562 to height 333: 593x333. Both odd.

6
00:00:43,200 --> 00:00:52,800
libx264: width not divisible by 2.

7
00:00:52,800 --> 00:01:01,710
Odd width alone fails: 427x240.

8
00:01:01,710 --> 00:01:17,750
-2 evens the width. Odd height alone still fails.

9
00:01:17,750 --> 00:01:22,070
scale=-2:334 gives 594x334.

10
00:01:22,070 --> 00:01:32,140
Exit code 0. 10 frames on disk.

11
00:01:32,140 --> 00:01:40,500
Same 593x333 frame, yuv444p: exit 0.

12
00:01:40,500 --> 00:01:51,640
yuv420p halves the color size. Only libx264 tested.

13
00:01:51,640 --> 00:02:02,470
Use -2 for width. Choose an even height.

14
00:02:02,470 --> 00:02:10,600
Not tested: other encoders, hardware encoders.
